# NAMES can span several 353 lines. The member list changes once, at 366,
# not line by line. Without away-notify a hidden WHOX follows, so away
# flags are known; its replies are not printed. Shapes from Ergo 2.19 with
# multi-prefix and userhost-in-names.
! welcome multi-prefix userhost-in-names
< :irc.test 005 textual CHANTYPES=# PREFIX=(qaohv)~&@%+ STATUSMSG=~&@%+ WHOX :are supported by this server
< :textual!~u@host.test JOIN #c
> MODE #c
? buffers = console #c
? joined #c
? members #c = textual
? line #c textual (~u@host.test) joined the channel
< :irc.test 353 textual = #c :@alice!a@h1 +bob!b@h2
? members #c = textual
< :irc.test 353 textual = #c :carol!c@h3 @+textual!~u@host.test
? members #c = textual
< :irc.test 366 textual #c :End of NAMES list
> WHO #c %tcuhnfa,152
? members #c = @alice @textual +bob carol
< :irc.test 354 textual 152 #c b h2 bob G+ 0
< :irc.test 354 textual 152 #c a h1 alice H@ alice
< :irc.test 315 textual #c :End of WHO list
? members #c = @alice @textual +bob(away) carol
# Nothing of NAMES or the hidden WHO was printed.
? lines #c 1
? lines console 3
? line console CHANTYPES=# PREFIX=(qaohv)~&@%+ STATUSMSG=~&@%+ WHOX are supported by this server
# A WHO the user asks for is printed, and a later NAMES sends no WHO.
< :irc.test 352 textual #c b h2 irc.test bob H+ :0 Bob
? line console #c b h2 irc.test bob H+ 0 Bob
? members #c = @alice @textual +bob(away) carol
< :irc.test 315 textual #c :End of WHO list
? line console #c End of WHO list
< :irc.test 353 textual = #c :@alice!a@h1 @+textual!~u@host.test
< :irc.test 366 textual #c :End of NAMES list
? members #c = @alice @textual
? registered textual
